Z||000000||Oreif||04-13-2000||10:28 PM||||I installed Eibach springs to lower my car 1". The question is, Does anyone who has lowered their car have an aftermarket rear sway bar installed? It looks like I'll have 2.5" to 3" from the sway bar mount (on the frame) to the ground. Does this pose a problem during normal driving? speed bumps? pulling in/out of driveways?  ||||reg||5
Z||000001||1FST2M6||04-14-2000||09:04 AM||||I have one... it doesn't pose any problem... my car scrapes going through the grocery store parking lot (speedbumps) but it's just the stock ground effects.. I'm running Konis and Eibachs, with bigger front and rear sway bars.. you'll be ok... ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||04-14-2000||01:27 PM||||My <BR>Formula is lowered about 1 1/2"(konis and eibachs) haven't had any probs yet||||reg||1
